,"createdAt":1775035003031,"changelog":"Fix: Updated TTS file path from /tmp/tts-*/ to /tmp/openclaw/tts-*/. Added safety check to always use latest file. Added workspace copy step for message tool compatibility.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[{"key":"ELEVENLABS_API_KEY","required":true}],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"zachgodsell93","slug":"meta-ads","displayName":"Meta Ads","summary":"Manage Meta (Facebook) Ads campaigns, ad sets, ads, creatives, and access performance metrics via full read/write API integration.","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.0"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":8036,"installs":216,"stars":30,"versions":1},"createdAt":1770005815556,"updatedAt":1779076586753,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770005815556,"changelog":"Initial release of Meta Ads API skill.\n\n- Full read/write integration with Meta (Facebook) Ads API.\n- Manage ad accounts, campaigns, ad sets, ads, and ad creatives.\n- Access detailed performance insights and metrics for accounts and campaigns.\n- Provides clear setup instructions, required permissions, and authentication steps.\n- Includes ready-to-use API request examples for all major ad management actions.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"thincher","slug":"minimax-understand-image","displayName":"minimax-understand-image","summary":"使用 MiniMax MCP 进行图像理解和分析。触发条件：(1) 用户要求分析图片、理解图像、描述图片内容 (2) 需要识别图片中的物体、文字、场景 (3) 使用 MiniMax 的 understand_image 功能","description":null,"topics":["图像"],"tags":{"latest":"1.0.3"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":8036,"installs":268,"stars":6,"versions":4},"createdAt":1771336689221,"updatedAt":1778991198217,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1771917444094,"changelog":"minimax-understand-image 1.0.3\n\n- 流程优化：首次配置流程更为简洁，后续可直接调用图像分析功能。\n- API Key 自动获取逻辑修改：默认从 ~/.openclaw/agents/main/agent/auth-profiles.json 查找，而非此前的路径。\n- 清理文档内容，去除冗余完整流程示例，提升可读性。\n- 步骤描述更明确，帮助用户更快完成配置和调用。","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"byungkyu","slug":"google-tasks-api","displayName":"Google Tasks","summary":"Google Tasks API integration with managed OAuth. Manage task lists and tasks with full CRUD operations. Use this skill when users want to read, create, update, or delete tasks and task lists in Google Tasks. For other third party apps, use the api-gateway skill (https://clawhub.ai/byungkyu/api-gateway). Calls run through the `maton` CLI with OAuth login, or over raw HTTP with a Maton API key where the CLI cannot be installed. Every call is authenticated as the user's connection and reaches only what that connection's authorization allows, which the provider enforces on every request; the endpoints documented here are the ones this skill uses, and any other endpoint of this app needs the user to ask for it by name. Default to read and list calls, and confirm every write or new connection with the user. This file also documents the three constructs that turn a Google Tasks connection into automation, in the order they are used: the connection (the first step), a hosted function that runs a Google Tasks action through the Maton SDK, and a trigger that calls that function on a schedule or on an event. Those sections are the platform's own reference text, shared with the api-gateway skill, with Google Tasks examples; they add no Google Tasks capability - Google Tasks is not an event source, a trigger cannot read Google Tasks data, and the files under `references/<source>/triggers.md` are the platform's event catalogues for the sources Maton offers (time, Calendly, GitHub, Gmail, HubSpot, Linear, Notion, Slack, Stripe).","description":null,"topics":["Api Integration"],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.5"},"stats":{"comments":1,"downloads":8029,"installs":254,"stars":10,"versions":14},"createdAt":1770463373833,"updatedAt":1790938200961,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790938058961,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","license":"MIT-0"},"metadata":{"setup":[],"os":null,"systems":null}},{"ownerHandle":"lobstergeneralintelligence","slug":"x-api","displayName":"X Api","summary":"Post to X (Twitter) using the official API with OAuth 1.0a. Use when you need to tweet, post updates, or publish content. Bypasses rate limits and bot detection that affect cookie-based approaches like bird CLI.","description":null,"topics":["Tweet"],"tags":{"latest":"0.1.0"},"stats":{"comments":5,"downloads":8024,"installs":282,"stars":45,"versions":1},"createdAt":1769635911554,"updatedAt":1778485867301,"latestVersion":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769635911554,"changelog":"- Initial release of x-api: post tweets to X (Twitter) using the official API with OAuth 1.0a.\n- Bypasses rate limits and bot detection—more reliable than cookie-based CLI tools.\n- Clear setup instructions for obtaining and configuring API credentials.\n- Supports multi-line tweet posts and returns the tweet URL on success.\n- Specifies API usage limits, troubleshooting steps, and distinguishes use cases vs. the bird CLI for reading.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"bastos","slug":"obsidian-daily","displayName":"Obsidian Daily","summary":"Manage Obsidian Daily Notes via obsidian-cli. Create and open daily notes, append entries (journals, logs, tasks, links), read past notes by date, and search vault content. Handles relative dates like \"yesterday\", \"last Friday\", \"3 days ago\".","description":null,"topics":[],"tags":{"latest":"1.2.1"},"stats":{"comments":0,"downloads":7990,"installs":272,"stars":5,"versions":4},"createdAt":1768264671758,"updatedAt":1778485733200,"latestVersion":{"version":"1.2.1","createdAt":1769695622938,"changelog":"No changes detected in this release.\n\n- Version 1.2.1 was published without any file or documentation changes.","license":null},"metadata":null},{"ownerHandle":"ivangdavila","slug":"skill-buil